Files: stage-2/ui/assets/wallet.js (the screen), kit.js (loads, status messages, the money-form behaviour, wallet summary), api.js (outcomes, 4 s abort, paging), money.js, retry.js, holds.js (authorizeForm, shared with /authorizations, D46).
What it does, by criterion:
  - W10.1 Numbers:
      - wallet-available is the headline; wallet-balance shows total; wallet-held is present only when held > 0;
      - each carries data-amount in minor units, with text from formatMoney (minor_units 0, 2 and 3; BigInt, no floats);
      - read from GET /me on every load.
  - W10.2 Pay form:
      - parseAmount follows D44: digits, an optional point and at most minor_units decimals. abc, 15.005, 1e3, -1, 1,5, empty, 0 and amounts above 1e9 minor units are refused in the page, with no request sent;
      - a note over 200 code points is refused the same way;
      - the visibility select;
      - a refusal (4xx with the envelope) shows pay-error with the server's message for people, keeps every input, and re-reads /me and /activity;
      - a success shows pay-success, keeps the values, and re-reads without a page reload;
      - the retry identity sends the same key and body while nothing changes; any input or change event mints a new key on the next submit;
      - pay-submit is disabled only while its own write is in flight.
  - W10.3 Uncertain outcomes:
      - a network failure, an abort at 4 s, a 5xx, or a response that is not the JSON envelope shows pay-uncertain, never pay-error;
      - the unchanged retry re-sends the same key and body; its success clears pay-uncertain and pay-error and re-reads the numbers and the feed.
  - W10.4 Request form on /: the same behaviour as pay, with request-error, request-uncertain and request-success.
  - W10.5 Feed:
      - activity-list, or empty-activity when nothing is visible;
      - items newest first as direct children, each with data-visibility, both handles, the exact amount and the note element (present when empty);
      - every page is read from the bare path, then ?offset=N&limit=200 (D64), and de-duplicated by payment_id;
      - text goes in through textContent only, so the I48 string shows literally.
  - W10.6 wallet-refresh:
      - never disabled;
      - each resource numbers its loads, and a response applies only when no later load of it has been applied, so the latest refresh wins;
      - the pay form's values are kept.
  - W10.7 Upgrade: the token lives in localStorage and is never re-issued, so an import of the same state keeps the page signed in. A 401 on an authenticated call ends the session (D65).
