Revision: 5f9781a, the same commit as W9 and W10. These screens were built with the UI in cabf1c3, and nothing in them changed after that.
Files: stage-2/ui/assets/requests.js, split-screen.js, split.js, holds.js, kit.js (loads, status messages, keepFocus), app.css.
What it does, by criterion:
  - W11.1 /requests:
      - incoming-list and outgoing-list, each with every request (all pages, D64);
      - every item has data-status and the exact amount;
      - pay and decline only on pending incoming requests, cancel only on pending outgoing ones;
      - each action disables only its own item's buttons while in flight, then re-reads the list;
      - empty-requests only when both lists are empty;
      - request-error with the server's message for a refusal, and the lists are re-read, so a request cancelled elsewhere loses its pay button;
      - request-uncertain on an unknown outcome. The re-read replaces it with the confirmed state once the item shows the action's status;
      - a request payment keeps its key per request for retries.
  - W11.2 /split:
      - split-preview shows the §9 shares in handle order before anything is posted (equalShares, the same rule as the server's);
      - split-error for an invalid amount, an empty, repeated or over-200 handle list (no request sent), and for server refusals such as the 404 for an unknown handle;
      - split-success; split-uncertain on an unknown outcome;
      - the retry identity, so an unchanged resubmission is the same key and body.
  - W11.3 /authorizations:
      - the authorize form, shared with / (D46): authorize-error, -success and -uncertain, with the retry identity;
      - the list newest first, each item with data-status, the exact amount, authorization-captured-{id} only when the status is captured, and the exact expires_at text;
      - the capture input is pre-filled with the remainder. Capture (for the receiver) and void (for the payer) appear only on open items and only for the party who may act;
      - after each action the item and the wallet numbers are re-read;
      - authorization-error for refusals (expired, not open, exceeds);
      - authorization-uncertain gives way to the captured state once the re-read shows it; a retry of a lost capture reuses its key;
      - empty-authorizations.
  - W11.4 Layout:
      - one column below 720 px; text wraps, and amounts stay on one line;
      - focus outlines 3 px; labelled controls;
      - no horizontal scroll at 375x812, 1024x768 or 1280x800 in every named state.
